1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,860
[music playing]
[音乐播放]

2
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:06,320
-Come and meet one of Africa's most unusual families.
-来见见非洲最不寻常的家庭之一

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,300
We've spent a whole year with a family of elephants
我们和大象一家共度了一年

4
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,460
raised by people.
由人抚养长大.

5
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:16,220
It's a family on a hazardous journey back into the wild.
这是一个家庭 在危险 旅程回到野外。

6
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:17,860
And this is their story.
这就是他们的故事。

7
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:24,300
-All of these elephants have been orphaned under traumatic
-所有这些大象都是在创伤中成为孤儿的

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,900
circumstances, having lost their families.
他们失去了家人

9
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,360
-Look at this little elephant.
-看看这只小象

10
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,280
How can you not adore him?
你怎么能不爱他?

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:41,720
-Will I ever forget an experience like this?
-威尔 我曾经忘记这样的经历吗?

12
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:57,600
-We just had a call that there's a little orphaned elephant
-我们刚接到一个电话,说有一只小孤象

13
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:01,120
that needs rescuing in Sam move.
这需要救援 在山姆移动。

14
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:04,340
-But being rescued is just the beginning.
- 但被救出来只是开始

15
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:09,080
-This is turning out to be much, much more difficult.
- 事实证明这要困难得多

16
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:10,080
-Good night, old baby.
-晚安,老宝贝.

17
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:22,440
-This is Nairobi National Park in Kenya.
-这是肯尼亚的内罗毕国家公园

18
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:26,960
And I'm here to meet a unique herd of rescued baby elephants.
我是来见一群获救的幼象的

19
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:31,080
All of them have had the worst possible start in life.
他们都有人生中最糟糕的开始

20
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,560
They've all lost their mothers.
他们都失去了母亲。

21
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:37,440
The leader of this little band of orphan toddlers is Wendy.
这个孤儿小队的首领是温蒂.

22
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:40,880
She's been here almost since the day she was born.
她从出生那天起就在这里

23
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:43,040
She never knew her mother, so everything she
她从来不认识她的母亲 所以她的一切

24
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:47,320
knows about being a baby elephant, she's learned from here.
她知道自己是小象 她从这里学的

25
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:50,880
She was only days old and still had her umbilical cord
她才几岁,还有脐带

26
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:53,080
attached when she was found.
当她被发现时被附着。

27
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:57,480
A band and daughter, her family fled from people.
一个乐队和女儿,她的家人逃离人们.

28
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,400
You wouldn't know from looking at her now,
你从现在看她就不会知道

29
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,200
but because she lost her mother at such a young age,
但是因为她这么年轻就失去了母亲

30
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:04,960
her immune system was extremely fragile.
她的免疫系统非常脆弱

31
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,080
She arrived in a very poor state.
她到达了一个非常贫穷的状态。

32
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:10,560
She got a blood transfusion from an older elephant
她从大象那里输血

33
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,800
which saved her life.
这救了她的命。

34
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:16,000
And now she's healthy, happy, and could be pretty mischievous.
而现在她健康,快乐, 并且可能相当邪恶。

35
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Get off my leg.
别碰我的腿

36
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,760
The only reason that Wendy and the others are alive
温蒂和其他人活着的唯一原因

37
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,960
is that they've been brought to an elephant nursery,
他们被带到了大象苗圃,

38
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,240
unlike any other.
和任何其他人不一样

39
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:34,560
This is a place where playing football
这里就是足球场

40
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:37,920
helps kickstart the recovery of broken-hearted babies.
帮助启动心碎婴儿的康复。

41
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:48,120
It's a place where bath time fun lends broken spirits
这是一个洗澡时间的乐趣借给破碎的灵魂的地方

42
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:51,800
and prepares shy orphans for their return to a life in the wild.
让害羞的孤儿在野外生活

43
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:57,360
It's a place where a team of devoted keepers
这是一个地方,一个团队 忠诚的守护者

44
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,640
become surrogate mothers,
成为代孕母亲,

45
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,200
sleeping next to vulnerable babies
睡在脆弱婴儿旁边

46
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,640
to give them the reassurance they desperately need.
让他们得到他们迫切需要的保证

47
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:10,120
All of these babies owe their lives
这些婴儿都欠他们一条命

48
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:12,800
to the vision of a remarkable woman.
给一个了不起的女人的梦想.

49
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:18,360
For 50 years, Daphne Sheldrick has helped nurse
50年来,Daphne Sheldrick帮助护士

50
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,480
orphaned elephants back to life.
孤儿大象复活.

51
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:26,760
Like many kenyans,
像许多肯亚人一样,

52
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:31,760
she's seen the devastating effect of decades of poaching on wild herds,
她看到了几十年偷猎对野生群群的毁灭性影响

53
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:35,560
and this is her way of giving something back to the elephants.
这是她把东西还给大象的方式

54
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:40,760
Over the years, Daphne and her team have rescued
多年来,Daphne和她的团队已经拯救了

55
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:42,760
more than a hundred baby elephants.
百余婴儿象.

56
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:49,760
As well as looking after their everyday physical needs,
除了照顾他们的日常身体需要,

57
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:52,560
she and her keepers have learned how to heal them.
她和守护者学会了如何治愈他们

58
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:55,560
To heal the emotional scars the babies carry
为了治好婴儿身上的伤疤

59
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:58,560
after losing their own families in the wild.
在野外失去家人后

60
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:10,560
The intensive care and safety of the nursery
幼儿保育和安全

61
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:13,560
is just the start of a hazardous journey
只是危险旅程的开始

62
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:17,560
designed to give baby elephants a second chance for a normal life.
为了给小象一个正常生活的第二次机会

63
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:21,560
But the nursery is not their final destination.
但托儿所不是他们的终点

64
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,560
The ultimate aim is to get them back into the wild.
最终目的是让他们回到野外.

65
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:28,560
But first, every one of these babies has to learn
但首先,每个婴儿都要学会

66
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:32,560
what it takes to be a free-living wild elephant.
做一只自由生活的野象需要什么?

67
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:37,560
The odds are stacked against them.
机会堆积在他们身上。

68
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:40,560
Only about half of the babies that are rescued
只有一半的婴儿获救

69
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,560
survive to see their second birthday.
活到二岁

70
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:49,560
But this is a story of hope.
但这是一个希望的故事。

71
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,560
So over the next year, I'll be getting to know some of the orphans
明年,我会认识一些孤儿

72
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,560
here at the nursery in Nairobi
在内罗毕的幼儿园

73
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:57,560
to see if these babies can recover from their loss
看看这些婴儿能否从损失中恢复过来

74
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:02,560
and start to learn the skills they need to live as wild adults.
并开始学习他们作为野生成年人生活所需的技能.

75
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:05,560
If they make it, they'll graduate to a release site
如果他们成功了,他们会毕业 到一个发布网站

76
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:08,560
in the wilds of Kenya's biggest national park
肯尼亚最大的国家公园的野外

77
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:12,560
where Jonathan is following the second stage of their story.
在那里乔纳森正在跟踪他们的故事的第二阶段。

78
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:31,560
This is Sarvo National Park, and we're about 350 kilometres a piece
这里是萨尔沃国家公园,我们大约每块350公里

79
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:34,560
of where Michaela is at the Nairobi orphanage.
麦可拉在内罗毕孤儿院

80
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:38,560
Sarvo is a huge chunk of Africa.
萨尔沃是一大块非洲.

81
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:40,560
It's an area the size of whales,
这是一个面积 鲸鱼,

82
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:43,560
and this is where the young orphans from Nairobi
这是来自内罗毕的年轻孤儿

83
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,560
are brought when they're ready to begin the gradual process
当他们准备好开始渐进过程时,他们就会被带来

84
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,560
of returning to the wild.
回到了野外。

85
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,560
This is perfect elephant country,
这是完美的大象国,

86
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:56,560
and it's home to Kenya's largest population of wild elephants,
这是肯尼亚最大的野象的家园,

87
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,560
10,000 of them living in a complex society
生活在复杂社会中的10,000人

88
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:03,560
dominated by mature females, the matriarchs.
以成熟的雌性为主 母性

89
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,560
The hope is that ultimately,
希望最终

90
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:07,560
the orphans come back to the world
孤儿们回到世界

91
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:10,560
and they live in the wilds of the wilds.
他们生活在野外

92
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:18,560
The hope is that ultimately,
希望最终

93
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,560
the orphans can one day join them
孤儿总有一天可以加入他们

94
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:23,560
and live a normal life in the African bush.
在非洲丛林里过正常生活

95
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:29,560
For the orphans, the journey from first being rescued
对于孤儿来说,从第一次被拯救的旅程

96
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:32,560
to finally returning to the wild is one of harsh lessons
终于回到野外 是残酷的教训之一

97
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,560
that can take several years to complete.
这需要几年的时间才能完成。

98
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,560
To see what it takes to make it,
来看看要做什么

99
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,560
I've come to meet an orphan that the keepers think
我是来见一个孤儿的 守护者们认为

100
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:42,560
is nearing the end of that journey.
旅程即将结束

101
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:46,560
This is Emily, and she's the matriarch of the orphan herd.
这是艾米丽,她是孤儿群的母权。

102
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:49,560
She had a really lousy start in life.
她有一个非常糟糕的开始 在生活中。

103
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,560
When she was just four weeks old,
当她才四个星期大的时候

104
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,560
she fell into a cesspit,
她掉进了粪坑,

105
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:55,560
and the stench of human waste caused her mother to reject her.
人类废物的臭味使她的母亲拒绝她。

106
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,560
In fact, not only did she reject her,
事实上 她不仅拒绝了她

107
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:00,560
she picked her up and tossed her through the air.
她把她捡起来 把她扔到空中

108
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:05,560
Luckily for her, she was rescued and taken to the Nairobi nursery.
幸运的是,她被救出并被带到内罗毕托儿所。

109
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:12,560
Emily is now 10, and the oldest elephant still being cared for here in Sarvo,
艾米丽现在已经十岁了 在萨尔沃,最年长的大象还在照顾中

110
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,560
but she's at a crossroads in her life.
但她正处在生命的十字路口

111
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,560
For the moment at least,
至少现在

112
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,560
she's helping 29 other orphans learn the ropes
她帮其他29个孤儿学绳子

113
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,560
and stay out of trouble.
别惹麻烦

114
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:24,560
But she's also old enough to leave the security of life
但是她年纪也够大了 可以离开生命的保障

115
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,560
with the keepers and the other orphans
与监护者和其他孤儿,

116
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:29,560
and start a family of her own back in the wild.
然后在野外建立她自己的家庭

117
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,560
The question is, when?
问题是,什么时候?

118
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:37,560
Over the next year, I hope to follow Emily's story
下一年,我希望跟随艾米莉的故事

119
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,560
and find the answer.
并找到答案。

120
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:41,560
First, I need to win her trust,
首先,我要赢得她的信任

121
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:44,560
so Emily's keepers are taking me to meet her
所以Emily的看守要带我去见她

122
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:46,560
to see if she likes the look of me.
看看她是否喜欢我

123
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:50,560
This is crunch time.
时间到了

124
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:53,560
I can feel my heart beating.
我能感觉到我的心跳。

125
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:56,560
Big meeting coming up.
重要会议即将到来。

126
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:59,560
There they come.
他们来了。

127
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,560
What a sight.
何等为观.

128
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,560
Beautiful.
美丽.

129
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,560
That big elephant in the middle.
中间那头大象

130
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,560
That must be Emily.
一定是艾米丽

131
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,560
Look, absolutely amazing.
你看,绝对惊人。

132
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,560
This is my first opportunity to see the Sarvo herd.
这是我第一次见到Sarvo群。

133
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:21,560
The first thing you notice is that virtually all of them are the same size,
你注意到的第一件事是,几乎所有的都是相同的尺寸,

134
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:24,560
and that's not what you would expect if it was a wild herd.
如果它是野生的畜群,那不是你所期望的。

135
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,560
And that's because all of them are orphans.
那是因为他们都是孤儿。

136
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:29,560
Just like the babies at the nursery with Michaela and Nairobi.
就像婴儿在托儿所 与迈克尔和内罗毕。

137
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:31,560
And they look.
他们看。

138
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,560
Look at them.
看看他们。

139
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,560
I can't quite believe I'm doing this.
我不敢相信我会这么做

140
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:44,560
I mean, I'm so used to being out in somewhere like the Masai Mara
我习惯像马赛玛拉一样出门

141
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:47,560
where you've got elephants that are wild, you stay in your car.
在那里,你有大象是野生的, 你留在你的车。

142
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:52,560
The last thing you'd want to do amongst elephants is be out on foot like this.
你最不想在大象中间做的事 就是这样走路

143
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:57,560
And if I say that Emily isn't, you know, she's barely a teenager,
如果我说Emily不是 她才十几岁

144
00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:00,560
but she is looking bigger and bigger.
但她看起来越来越大了.

145
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:04,560
In fact, I don't think I need the knockless anymore.
事实上,我再也不需要无敌了

146
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:26,560
It's really important that Emily accepts me.
艾米丽接受我很重要

147
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:30,560
So at some point, I'm hoping that she'll come and introduce herself to me.
所以我希望她能来自我介绍一下

148
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:33,560
And then hopefully, I'll become one of the herd.
希望之后,我会成为群之一。

149
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:38,560
Because without her acceptance, I haven't got a chance of really following the story.
因为没有她的接受, 我还没有机会 真正跟踪的故事。

150
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:42,560
Whoops.
呜呼.

151
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:44,560
Uh-oh.
哦,哦,我刚说到

152
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,560
She is suddenly looking very big.
她突然变大了

153
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:56,560
If she wanted to, she could really do me some damage.
如果她想的话,她真的会伤害我

154
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:59,560
So I have to take this nice and easy.
所以我得慢慢来

155
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:25,560
I can actually feel her breath just breathing down my throat.
我其实能感觉到她的呼吸 只是呼吸在我的喉咙。

156
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,560
Just praying, Emily.
只是祈祷,艾米丽。

157
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:36,560
Okay, what's that decision?
好吧,这是什么决定?

158
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:13,560
Well, speechless.
嗯,无语。

159
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:19,560
I don't know what she was saying to me, but that was pretty amazing, I can tell you.
我不知道她在对我说什么, 但这是相当惊人的,我可以告诉你。

160
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:24,560
Incredible.
不可思议.

161
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:29,560
I think it's going to be okay, but who knows?
我觉得会好起来的 但谁知道呢?

162
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:37,560
Here at the nursery in Nairobi is where the journey back into the wild begins.
在内罗毕的幼稚园 回到野外的旅程从此开始

163
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:42,560
No one knows when or where the next baby is going to need rescuing,
没人知道下一个孩子何时何地需要拯救

164
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,560
so the team here is always on standby.
所以这里的团队总是待命。

165
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:54,560
Keepers like Edwin dedicate their lives to helping these traumatised babies.
爱德温这样的守护者 毕生致力于帮助这些受创伤的婴儿

166
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:58,560
Six years ago, he hoped to be a priest.
六年前,他希望能成为牧师.

167
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:01,560
Now his life revolves around baby elephants.
现在他的生活围绕着小象.

168
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:08,560
Like many of the keepers, before working here, he'd never even set eyes on an elephant.
和很多守护者一样,在这里工作之前,他甚至从来没有看到一只大象.

169
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,560
Let alone looked after one.
更别提照顾了

170
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:15,560
But now you'd think he was born to it.
但现在你认为他是天生的

171
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:21,560
Just look at this scene, you can see that these elephants have such a strong bond with their keepers.
看看这个场景,你可以看到这些大象与他们的守护者有如此牢固的联系.

172
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:25,560
And at this nursery stage, the keepers are vital to the orphans.
而在这个育婴阶段,守护者对孤儿至关重要.

173
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:31,560
They're within 24 hours a day, they give them love, attention, they nurture them, they feed them, they sleep with them.
他们一天24小时之内,给他们爱,关注,培育,喂养,和他们同床共枕.

174
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:35,560
It's so lovely to see.
真可爱

175
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:42,560
It's the bond between the keepers and elephants that helps make this place so unique.
守护者与大象之间的纽带 有助于使这个地方变得如此独特

176
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:47,560
And it's the key to their success with these sensitive and vulnerable young babies.
它是他们成功的关键 与这些敏感和脆弱的年轻婴儿.

177
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:55,560
Hello? Yes.
有人吗? 对

178
00:12:56,560 --> 00:13:03,560
We've got a rescue down in Samboru. Guys, it's not like we're in there.
桑波鲁有救援行动 伙计们,这不是像我们在那里。

179
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,560
It's definitely not.
绝对不是。

180
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:14,560
Yes, okay, we'll shoot for five o'clock. Is the pilot there?
是的,好吧,我们会拍摄 五点钟。 飞行员在吗?

181
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:18,560
The rescue is being coordinated by Daphne's daughter, Angela.
救援工作由达芙妮的女儿安吉拉协调.

182
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,560
Thank you, we'll be there soon.
谢谢,我们马上就到

183
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:31,560
As an emergency flight is being organised, the keepers led by Edwin loaded truck with essential supplies needed for the rescue and head out to Nairobi's Wilson Airport.
在组织紧急航班时,Edwin率领的护卫人员将救援所需的必需品装上卡车,前往内罗毕的威尔逊机场。

184
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:48,560
The call has come from the Samboru National Reserve a couple of hours away by plane.
电话来自Samboru国家储备区 几小时后乘飞机过来

185
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:54,560
What's happened is that a baby elephant has been discovered alone and in trouble.
发生的事情是一只小象被单独发现,并陷入困境.

186
00:13:54,560 --> 00:14:02,560
She's lost both her own mother and her entire family group and is trying to latch on to any other herd she can find.
她失去了自己的母亲和她整个家庭 并试图抓住其他任何她能找到的牧群

187
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:06,560
But all she's getting is rejection.
但她只得到拒绝

188
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:11,560
At just a few months old, she's still totally dependent on milk.
才几个月,她仍然完全依赖牛奶。

189
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:18,560
Some can temple show that she hasn't fed for days and is suffering from severe dehydration.
有些神庙可以表明她已经好几天没吃东西了,并患有严重的脱水症.

190
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:31,560
A mother pushes her away, anxious to defend her own baby from this little stranger.
母亲把她推开 急于保护自己的孩子 远离这个陌生人

191
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:38,560
All alone and totally rejected, she has no food or protection.
她独自一人被彻底拒绝,没有食物或保护。

192
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:44,560
If she doesn't starve to death, she'll be an easy target for predators.
如果她不饿死,她就会成为捕食者容易的目标.

193
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:49,560
Without her mother, her life hangs in the balance.
没有她的母亲,她的生命就悬在平衡之中.

194
00:14:49,560 --> 00:15:00,560
Back in Nairobi, not a second is wasted in getting airborne.
回到内罗毕,一秒钟都没空

195
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:08,560
But even as they take off, the keepers have no way of knowing if they can get to her in time.
但是,即使他们起飞, 看守者没有办法 知道他们是否能及时找到她。

196
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:20,560
The abandoned baby is still trying to follow a herd as they cross a river swollen by recent rains.
被抛弃的婴儿仍然在试图跟随一个牧群,当他们渡过最近因降雨而肿胀的河流时.

197
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:27,560
Despite their hostility, the little elephant can't resist following them.
尽管有敌意,小象还是无法抗拒跟随他们.

198
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:32,560
But she's taking a huge risk.
但她冒着巨大的风险

199
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:38,560
The baby elephants are sometimes separated from their mothers as they've tried to cross fast-flowing rivers.
小象有时在试图穿越快速流淌的河流时与母亲分开.

200
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:43,560
And in fact, this could have been how she lost her own family.
事实上,这可能是她失去家人的原因。

201
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:53,560
On board, the rescue playing with Edwin and the other keepers is a Kenyan wildlife services event.
与Edwin和其他守护者一起进行的救援活动是肯尼亚野生动物服务活动。

202
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:59,560
They have to find the orphan as quickly as possible.
他们必须尽快找到孤儿

203
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:05,560
They're getting late and soon lions and hyenas will be looking for an easy kill.
他们越来越迟了,很快狮子和土狼会寻找一个容易的杀戮.

204
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:09,560
But they're still an hour's drive away from the river.
但他们离河还有一小时路程

205
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:15,560
Meanwhile, the little orphan is now gambling with her life.
与此同时,这个小孤儿 正在赌她的生命。

206
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:19,560
She's being overwhelmed.
她被压抑了

207
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:24,560
She really needs the bigger elephants to help her.
她真的需要更大的大象来帮助她.

208
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:29,560
But instead, they're pushing her away.
但相反,他们把她推开.

209
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:41,560
This seems like a harsh reaction, but taking on a needy, unrelated baby would jeopardise their own family's future.
这似乎是一个严酷的反应, 但拿一个需要的,无关紧要的婴儿 会危及他们自己家庭的未来。

210
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:50,560
With darkest approaching, she's in deep trouble.
随着最黑暗的接近, 她陷入了深渊。

211
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:56,560
Her only hope lies with Edwin and the rescue team, but they can find her in time.
她唯一的希望在于埃德温和救援队,但他们可以及时找到她.

212
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:10,560
For the babies already at the Nairobi Nursery, the chaos of their rescues is behind them, but the trauma lives on.
对于已经在内罗毕托儿所的婴儿来说,他们营救的混乱已经过去了,但创伤还在继续。

213
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:18,560
Like all babies, they thrive on routine, and here it helps men shattered lives.
和所有婴儿一样,他们靠例行公事繁衍,在这里,它帮助男人破坏生活。

214
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:21,560
So each day follows a set pattern.
所以,每一天都遵循既定的模式。

215
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:28,560
When they first arrive, some of the orphans are so distressed after losing their mothers.
当他们第一次到来时,一些孤儿在失去母亲后感到非常痛苦。

216
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:32,560
They simply give up the struggle to live.
他们只是放弃了生活的斗争。

217
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:39,560
But friendships formed with the other little ones here can make the difference between life and death.
但与这里其他小人结成的友谊,可以改变生死.

218
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,560
This is where Wendy comes in.
这是温蒂进来的地方。

219
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:47,560
The nursery encourages the orphans to live as they should in the wild.
托儿所鼓励孤儿在野外生活。

220
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:56,560
So just as a wild herd has its matriarch, the baby herd has its own mini matriarch, Wendy.
所以,就像一个野生的牧群有它的母性, 婴儿牧群有自己的小母性,温蒂。

221
00:17:57,560 --> 00:18:05,560
This has got her big heart and takes any newcomers under her wing, mothering them until they can gain their confidence.
这得到了她的大心脏 并带走任何新来者 在她的翅膀下,母亲他们 直到他们能够获得他们的信心。

222
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:16,560
The younger babies look up to her, and Wendy's natural affection helps fill the emotional void left by losing their own mothers.
年幼的婴儿仰慕她,温蒂的自然感情通过失去自己的母亲,帮助填补了留下的情感空白.

223
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:24,560
Throughout the day, the elephants move around so that they can graze on different foods.
整天,大象们到处移动,以便他们可以用不同的食物放牧.

224
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:34,560
She also gives them a chance to get to know each other and work as a herd and sort out what their role is, although Wendy here is always the leader.
她还给了他们一个了解彼此的机会,并作为一个牧群工作,整理出他们的角色是什么,虽然这里的温蒂总是领导者.

225
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:38,560
This is basically what would happen with a wild herd of elephants.
这基本上就是一头野生大象的结局。

226
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:46,560
The big difference is though, in the wild it would be a herd with lots of different ages, and the leader would be an old female of at least 50 plus.
最大的区别是,在野外,它会是一个有着许多不同年龄的群,领导者将是至少50加的老雌性.

227
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:52,560
Here it's a bunch of orphans, and an elephant less than two years old has to take responsibility.
这里有一群孤儿,一头不到两岁的大象必须承担责任.

228
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:57,560
Wendy's always ready to welcome any new arrival.
Wendy随时愿意欢迎任何新的到来

229
00:18:57,560 --> 00:19:02,560
Provided an orphaned baby can survive long enough to reach the nursery.
如果孤儿能活到孩子出生为止。

230
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:12,560
Back in Samboru, things are going from bad to worse.
回到桑波鲁,事情变得更糟

231
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:23,560
By the time the rescue team finds the abandoned baby, it's too dark to fly her out, and if they can't capture her, Edwin knows she's unlikely to survive the night.
到了救援队找到被抛弃的婴儿时,已经太黑了,无法将她飞出,如果他们无法抓住她,埃德温知道她不可能在夜晚存活.

232
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:33,560
She may be weak and starving, but fear gives her the strength to run for her life. The team can't risk losing her.
她可能身体虚弱,饥饿,但恐惧让她有力量逃命. 团队不能冒险失去她.

233
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:43,560
It's the wildlife vet who manages to catch her.
是野生兽医抓到她的

234
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:50,560
She's so scared they need to cover her head with a blanket to calm her down.
她很害怕 他们需要用毯子遮住她的头 让她冷静下来

235
00:19:55,560 --> 00:20:02,560
As the vet checks her out, the priority is to get some rehydration fluid into her.
当兽医检查她出来时 首要任务是给她注入一些补液

236
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:06,560
Probably the first proper drink she's had since losing her mother.
可能是她失去母亲后第一次喝的好酒

237
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:13,560
If she doesn't take the bottle, they could lose her in the night.
如果她不拿瓶子, 他们可能会失去她 在夜晚。

238
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:41,560
For Emily's herd of older orphans, the routine of daily life in Sarvo follows a similar pattern to the one they grew up with in the Nairobi nursery.
对于Emily的老孤儿群来说,萨尔沃的日常生活模式与他们在内罗毕托儿所长大的模式类似。

239
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:56,560
At first light, the keepers let the elephants out from the safety of their overnight stock aides.
一开始,守夜者让大象们离开他们过夜的库存辅助工具的安全.

240
00:20:56,560 --> 00:21:03,560
They then take a step back and Emily takes charge.
然后他们退一步 Emily负责.

241
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:12,560
Elephants live as long as we do and go through the same stages of life at the same time as us, so all these youngsters are really just children.
大象的寿命和我们一样长, 经历与我们相同的生命阶段, 所以所有这些年轻人都是孩子。

242
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:17,560
They still need the guidance of an older elephant like Emily.
他们仍然需要像艾米莉这样的老象的指导.

243
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:43,560
[Music]
[音乐]

244
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:46,560
That's a pretty good way to start the morning, isn't it?
这是一个相当好的方式 开始上午,不是吗?

245
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:51,560
They're stretching, rubbing. They've got food to hand as well.
他们伸展,擦伤。 他们还有食物要交

246
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:59,560
[Music]
[音乐]

247
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:16,560
[Music]
[音乐]

248
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:26,560
With Emily leading in protecting the orphans, every day spent in the park brings them a step closer to becoming wild elephants again.
随着艾米莉带头保护孤儿,每天花在公园里,使他们更接近再次成为野生大象.

249
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:41,560
Now here in Sarvo, the elephants are allowed to roam completely wild, so this is their first chance to really find out what is or isn't dangerous out in the bush.
在萨尔沃,大象们可以游荡在野外, 所以这是他们第一次有机会真正发现 丛林里有什么危险或并不危险。

250
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:45,560
The keepers are still here, but they're very much more in the background.
守护者们还在这里,但他们在背景方面却更加深入.

251
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:52,560
Each day is different because there's no knowing who or what they'll meet next.
每一天都是不同的,因为不知道他们接下来会遇到谁或什么.

252
00:22:55,560 --> 00:23:03,560
This time it's just the neighbours, a herd of curious giraffe, but in thick stuff like this, the young orphans need to be on their guard.
这一次只是邻居,一群好奇的长颈鹿, 但是在这样厚厚的东西中, 年轻的孤儿需要小心。

253
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:15,560
And if there is something or someone new, the herd can usually rely on Emily to be the first in.
如果有新人或新人 牧群通常可以依靠艾米莉成为第一

254
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:22,560
Emily just checking us out.
艾米丽只是检查我们出去。

255
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:46,560
[Music]
[音乐]

256
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:51,560
I suppose you could describe this as the equivalent of an elephant handshake.
我想你可以说这相当于大象握手.

257
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:57,560
You can feel her just blowing warm air back up to me.
你可以感觉到她只是吹 温暖的空气回来给我。

258
00:23:57,560 --> 00:24:01,560
It's amazing that trunk.
这箱子真神奇

259
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:07,560
She can do anything she wants with her.
她可以随心所欲

260
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:14,560
And of course if she wanted to, she could just pick me up and throw me away, but she's so gentle.
当然,如果她想, 她可以只是接我 并把我扔了, 但她是如此温柔。

261
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:26,560
I don't think she liked the way I tied my laces up.
我觉得她不喜欢我把鞋带绑起来的方式

262
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:38,560
You know, it's wonderful to feel her relaxing enough to allow me to join her herd.
感觉她放松得让我加入她的队伍真好

263
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:47,560
It means I can get really close to her over the coming months as she decides whether she's going to stay with the orphans or head back to the wild.
意思是在未来的几个月里 我可以和她很亲近 当她决定要和孤儿在一起 还是回野外去

264
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:55,560
[Music]
[音乐]

265
00:24:55,560 --> 00:25:00,560
In Nairobi, Daphne and the keepers are waiting for news of the little Samburu baby.
在内罗毕,Daphne和守护者正在等待 小Samburu婴儿的消息。

266
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:03,560
Do you have a chest?
你有胸吗?

267
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,560
Yeah.
对

268
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:07,560
He is stressed.
他压力很大。

269
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:12,560
Everyone fears the worst, but preparations are being made hoping for the best.
每个人都最害怕,但人们正准备着希望最好的。

270
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:20,560
If she does make it, she'll be desperately hungry, so a unique milk formula pioneered by Daphne is made ready.
如果她成功了,她会非常饥饿, 所以一个独特的牛奶配方 由Daphne开创了。

271
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:29,560
The keepers try to anticipate her physical needs, but no one knows what state she'll be in emotionally.
守护者试图预测她的生理需求,但没有人知道她会处于何种情绪状态.

272
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:41,560
Back in Samburu, the morning brings good news. The little orphan has survived the night, but now she has to be sedated for her flight to Nairobi.
回到桑布鲁,早上带来好消息。 小孤儿在夜里幸存了下来,但现在她必须被镇静服药才能飞往内罗毕.

273
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:44,560
A plane is no place for a traumatised elephant.
飞机不是受创伤的大象的地方

274
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:56,560
Despite a sleepless night, Edwin can't relax for a moment.
尽管一夜无眠,埃德温暂时无法放松.

275
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:06,560
He's constantly checking on the latest addition to his orphan family to ensure that she's still breathing.
他不停地检查他孤儿家庭的最新增加,以确保她还活着.

276
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:09,560
Too much anesthetic could kill her.
太多麻醉剂会害死她

277
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:25,560
As soon as they touch down, there's a truck from the nursery waiting to take her to her new home.
一旦他们触摸下来,有一辆卡车 从苗圃等待带她到新家。

278
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:35,560
They rush her straight to the nursery, desperate to get her to safety before she starts to wake up.
急着赶她去托儿所 迫不及待地想在她醒来前把她送去安全的地方

279
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:46,560
As the nursery's newest member arrives, she's welcomed by Daphne.
随着托儿所最新的成员到来,她受到达芙妮的欢迎.

280
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:55,560
She decides to put her into the stable next to Wendy, hoping that the mini matriarch will be able to comfort and reassure her.
她决定把她放到温蒂旁边的马厩里,希望小母狗能够安慰和安抚她.

281
00:26:58,560 --> 00:27:10,560
As she comes round, matrices are on hand to stop her hurting herself, as she panics at all the strange sights and smells.
当她转身时,母体在手 阻止她伤害自己, 她惊慌失措 在所有奇怪的视觉和气味。

282
00:27:10,560 --> 00:27:17,560
She's naturally confused and very frightened by all the people around her.
她自然感到困惑,被周围所有人吓坏了.

283
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:23,560
She's also suffering from the after effects of the anesthetic, so anything could happen.
她也患有麻醉剂的后遗症,所以什么都可能发生.

284
00:27:27,560 --> 00:27:35,560
This is the first real chance to see what state she's in and if her ordeal has left any lasting physical damage.
这是第一个真正的机会 看看她处于什么状态 以及她的折磨是否留下了 任何持久的身体损害。

285
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:42,560
After two days without sleep, Edwin hands her over to the other keepers.
在两天没睡觉后,埃德温把她交给其他看守人.

286
00:27:42,560 --> 00:27:47,560
With coaxing, she accepts a much needed drink of milk.
她接受非常需要的牛奶饮料

287
00:27:47,560 --> 00:27:52,560
It's a good sign, but she's by no means out of danger yet.
这是个好兆头 但她还没有脱离危险

288
00:27:55,560 --> 00:28:03,560
She's still clinging to life, but she could so easily have caught deadly pneumonia from the flooded river.
她仍然坚持生命, 但她可以很容易地 感染致命肺炎 从淹没的河流.

289
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:14,560
The keepers have decided to call her "Nesarian," "Samburu" for "Lucky One." Only time will tell if that's true.
守护者们决定称她为"内萨里安","桑布鲁"为"幸运一号". 只有时间才能知道这是真的

290
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:20,560
Right now, the only certainty is that the next 24 hours are going to be critical.
现在,唯一确定的是 接下来的24小时将是关键的。

291
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:31,560
Tomorrow on Elephant Daris, there's a big move ahead for Wendy and the older Nairobi orphans.
明天在达里斯大象上 温蒂和内罗毕的老孤儿还有一大步

292
00:28:31,560 --> 00:28:37,560
In Sarvo, how will Emily react when her herd encounters wild elephants?
在Sarvo,当Emily遇到野生大象时,会有什么反应?

293
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:45,560
And will Nesarian win her battle for life?
奈萨利安能赢得生命之战吗?
